Interactive USD change of the arnold type of a linked light

A sphere light, the only light of the scene, is linked to the left of two spheres. A spot shaping is added to it,
changing its arnold type, and removed, the right sphere is added to its light link collection, an occluder invisible to
the camera shadows the right sphere, the shaping is added again with a shadow link excluding it, and the right sphere is
removed from the light link collection. The stage is re-rendered after each edit. Covers the fix of the light type
change with light linking (#2663).
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
